# =============================================================================
# Swiss Reality Check — Hack Apertus, Track 1B
#
# Three things are ignored here, and the reasons are load-bearing enough to
# spell out:
#
#   1. Secrets.        src/eval/.env holds API keys. Never committed.
#   2. Derived data.   Run artefacts that a re-run regenerates: raw model
#                      output, intermediate parse stages, vector caches.
#   3. Model weights.  A GGUF is several GB and must never enter git.
#
# The EVIDENCE is deliberately tracked. Four subtrees under results/ are what a
# reader checks the claims against; a submission whose numbers cannot be
# audited is asking for trust rather than reporting a result.
# =============================================================================

# ---- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
*.env
!.env.example
!src/eval/.env.example

# ---- derived run artefacts ---------------------------------------------------
# By default nothing under results/ is tracked: raw model output and the
# intermediate stages are regenerated by re-running and are large.
#
# Two details of the syntax are load-bearing:
#
#   1. `results/*`, NOT `results/`. A trailing slash excludes the directory
#      itself, and git cannot re-include anything beneath an excluded directory
#      -- so that form keeps the evidence directories ignored no matter what the
#      `!` lines say. `*` leaves the parent un-excluded, which is what makes the
#      negations legal.
#   2. Git is last-match-wins, so these negations must sit BELOW every other
#      pattern that could match them. Position is the mechanism, not style.
results/*
!results/final_scores/
!results/charts/
!results/narrative/
!results/test_run/

# Regenerated on every run; large and not evidence.
results/raw_responses/
results/logs/
results/parsed/
results/scores/

# ---- derived RAG artefacts ---------------------------------------------------
# The chunk corpus is rebuilt byte-identically from the tracked data/sources/
# raw_pages/ files by `python src/fix/rag/prepare_corpus.py`. Tracking it would
# add ~460 KB of duplication that can only go stale.
src/fix/rag/corpus/
# RAG run outputs. Mock-backend self-tests, and a tracked results_rag_*.json is
# exactly the file someone later quotes as a result.
src/fix/rag/results_rag_*.json
# Dense-retrieval vector caches. Regenerated from the corpus; multi-MB binaries.
src/fix/rag/**/*.npz
*.npz

# ---- seal state --------------------------------------------------------------
# The recorded hash is tracked. The access log and the freeze are run-time state
# that must be visible to anyone auditing the run, so both are tracked too.
src/eval/seal/access.log.preflight-incident

# ---- submission artefacts ----------------------------------------------------
# The demo video is large and is uploaded through the submission form rather
# than committed. Its size and SHA-256 are recorded in README.md so the uploaded
# file can be verified.
brag-output/
models/
hf_dataset/
logs/

# ---- python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.venv/
venv/
env/
# Anchored to the repo root so a same-named directory inside src/ is not
# swallowed by accident.
/build/
/dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.tox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# ---- notebooks ---------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- IDE ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# ---- model weights and indexes ----------------------------------------------
*.gguf
*.gguf.split-*
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.h5
faiss_index/
*.faiss
.cache/
huggingface/

# ---- OS ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db

# ---- editor backups ----------------------------------------------------------
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak
*~
